# ── Frontend / browser-exposed — bundled into the client JS by Vite ──
# NOT secret: anyone can read these from the live site's page source (the
# Supabase key is the public "anon" key — real protection is Row Level
# Security, not keeping this hidden). These are what need to be set in
# Vercel's Environment Variables for production. When adding one there,
# pick type "Config", not "Secret" — Vercel will warn if you pick "Secret"
# for a VITE_-prefixed var, since "Secret" means "never readable again
# after saving," which is a contradiction for something that ends up
# exposed in the browser anyway.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-anon-key
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id

# Optional — Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (format: G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# Only loaded client-side after a visitor consents to analytics cookies
# (see CookieConsentContext). Leave unset and the consent banner/preferences
# UI still work, they just have nothing to actually turn on.
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ── Everything below is NOT read from this file ──
# These are Supabase Edge Function secrets (Deno.env.get(...) inside
# supabase/functions/*), not Vite frontend env vars. Vite only bundles
# VITE_-prefixed variables into the browser build, so real values here would
# be both a leak risk (this file is committed to git) and functionally inert
# (the edge functions never read it). Set the real values as Edge Function
# Secrets — via the Supabase dashboard, `supabase secrets set`, or Lovable AI
# for this Lovable-managed project. This section exists purely as a reference
# for which secrets the project needs.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# ADMIN_EMAIL=
# DARAJA_CONSUMER_KEY=
# DARAJA_CONSUMER_SECRET=
# DARAJA_SHORTCODE=
# DARAJA_PASSKEY=
# DARAJA_CALLBACK_URL=